# The units of llama-dspark that make one program, in the order they are
# linked.
#
# The order is bytewise and is part of the list rather than left to
# whoever runs it.  The first unit is the one the rest are linked into,
# so the order decides which declarations are read and which are
# imported, and what a link refuses changes with it: the same 52 units
# refuse 238 in this order and 249 in the order the shell sorts them in,
# which depends on the locale.
#
# 51 units.  What is left out, and why, is at the end.
